  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 453 AM MDT WED OCT 21 2026\nDrying conditions and near normal temperatures will return for \nthe weekend thanks to a building ridge of high pressure over the\nWest Coast. By late Sunday, long range forecast models have \nonce again converged on a closed low pressure system moving \nonshore and slowly east over the area through the early part of \nnext week. This pattern would bring cooler and wetter conditions\nyet again by early next week. The highest chances for \nprecipitation would be over the west-central Idaho mountains. \nWith how highly variable and volatile the synoptic pattern has \nbeen even just within 24 hours of this forecast, forecaster \nconfidence is low at this time.",
